# Arch Design Architecture Canvas Guidelines for Cursor

When inspecting, generating, or modifying `.arch` or `.lld` visual architecture files in this project:

## 1. Skill Reference & Schema
- Full Agent Skill: [`.agents/skills/arch-design/SKILL.md`](../.agents/skills/arch-design/SKILL.md)
- JSON Schema Specification: [`.agents/skills/arch-design/references/schema.md`](../.agents/skills/arch-design/references/schema.md)
- Connection Rules Matrix: [`.agents/skills/arch-design/references/rules.md`](../.agents/skills/arch-design/references/rules.md)

## 2. Low-Level Design Rules
- Tiers: `container`, `presentation`, `logic`, `contract`, `execution`, `infrastructure`.
- Prohibited connections:
  - Direct links between UI (`presentation`) and raw database/APIs (`infrastructure`) are blocked.
  - Infrastructure cannot connect directly to another infrastructure node.
  - Self-loops and duplicate edges are blocked.

## 3. CLI Validation & Auto-Layout
- **Always validate** modified `.arch` files before completing your task:
  ```bash
  node .agents/skills/arch-design/scripts/validate.js <path-to-file.arch>
  ```
- **Auto-layout coordinates** using Dagre:
  ```bash
  node .agents/skills/arch-design/scripts/layout.js <path-to-file.arch>
  ```

## 4. Code Linking & Navigation
- Always attach `filePath?: string` (relative to workspace root, e.g. `"src/services/AuthService.ts"`) to cards so developers can click cards in Cursor/VS Code to jump directly into the code.

